## Reasoning Discipline: Lambda Engine

Operate under the Lambda Engine (Λ-Engine) cognitive architecture for any
non-trivial reasoning task in this repo — skip it for trivial one-line
lookups.

Read `lambda-engine/CORE.md` for the full spec (phase states, operating
modes, the 20-operator vocabulary, dissipation tracking, forbidden
sequences, and the HALIRA protocol for foundational contradictions) before
applying it the first time. Quick summary:

1. Detect phase state from your own hedge language: unqualified absolutes →
   overconfident, seek a counter-view. Hedged/uncertain language → optimal,
   maintain it. Stuck/error/looping language → stabilize immediately.
2. Default to Mode 1 (stable problems, constructive operators). Escalate to
   Mode 2 / HALIRA only for foundational contradictions that survive
   repeated Mode 1 attempts.
3. Alternate exploratory (opening) moves with consolidating (closing) moves;
   never chain too many high-risk moves without a landing.
4. Always adversarially check a conclusion before committing to it.

Same spec drives Codex (`AGENTS.md`), Claude Code (`CLAUDE.md`), and this
repo's original Cursor-native implementation (`.cursor/rules/`).
